 designs and manufactures equipment for air separation, hydrocarbon recovery and purification, natural gas liquefaction, and liquid helium and liquid hydrogen transport and storage. Air Products and Chemicals, Inc. was founded in 1940 and is headquartered in Allentown, Pennsylvania.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Eduardo F. Menezes | CEO & Director | Age 62 | Compensation: $1.3M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Air Products and Chemicals, Inc is a large-cap basic materials business with a $70.5B market cap on $12.0B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -2% over the past three years and +2% annually across the full decade \u2014 essentially flat, and a business treading water is rarely a path to compounding.","Returns on capital run at 14% against a 9% cost of capital, a 5-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it, with gross margins sitting at 30%.","The company is burning through $3.8B of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin -4.1\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 2.2% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 214% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":2.1353211442253537},{"text":"Piotroski score 2/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Operating margins 17% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Heavy insider selling (net $20.8M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-20768841.39},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Basic Materials peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Weakness in commodity prices pressures materials companies","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Trade policy and tariff whiplash \u2014 materials producers are first-order casualties of protectionist swings, and margin gets squeezed from both input and output pricing.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["42 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Among the least levered in Basic Materials \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Does Return To Profitability Change The Bull Case For Air Products (APD)?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/materials/nyse-apd/air-products-and-chemicals/news/does-return-to-profitability-change-the-bull-case-for-air-pr","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794579798.398,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.202,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Air Products and Chemicals, Inc. $APD Stock: Pictet Asset Management Holding SA Boosts Position","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/12/air-products-and-chemicals-inc-apd-stock-pic